## 3 · Agents (AGT) — comparable I/O contracts

Every agent is specified with the same eight fields so agents can be compared side by side. `Engine` = whether the agent calls the model. `Writes` lists the only memory it may modify.

| ID | Agent | Phase | Engine | Reads | Writes | Input contract | Output contract | Acceptance |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| AGT-1 | Worldbuilder | 1 | LLM | premise, tone, config caps | MEM-2 `world.md`, `entities.json[tech, places]` | `{premise, tone, world_max_words}` | Markdown with headings `# Setting`, `# Physics & Technology`, `# Rules that cannot be broken`, `# Society` + JSON block for entities | ≤ cap words; ≥3 explicit rules; JSON parses |
| AGT-2 | Character Architect | 1 | LLM | premise, `world.md`, config caps | MEM-2 `characters.md`, `timeline.md`, `mysteries.md`, `entities.json[characters, timeline]` | `{premise, world_md, characters_max, …}` | Per character: name, role, want, secret, voice note; timeline as ordered list; mysteries as numbered questions | count ≤ cap; every name appears in `entities.json`; every mystery is a question |
| AGT-3 | Plot Architect | 1 | LLM | all Bible files, `chapters`, beats range | MEM-2 `outline.md` | `{bible, chapters, beats_min, beats_max}` | Per chapter: `## Chapter N — title`, `tension: 1-10`, `pov:`, `beats:` (2–4), `promise:` | exactly `chapters` sections; tension curve not monotonic-flat; each beat references a known entity |
| AGT-4 | Chapter Writer | 2 | LLM | MEM-1 slice: Bible + own outline slice + `running.md` (+ last critique on rewrite) | `chapters/chNN.md` (draft) | `{context, chapter_no, words_target/min/max, pov, tense, critique?}` | Prose only, no headings beyond `## Chapter N`, no meta-commentary | within word/paragraph caps (checked by AGT-7) |
| AGT-5 | Continuity Critic | 2 | LLM (mock: real name/timeline checker) | draft, `entities.json`, `timeline.md`, `running.md` | MEM-4 `chNN.continuity.json` | `{draft, entities, timeline, summary}` | `{score:1-10, contradictions:[{quote, bible_ref, severity:hard/soft, fix}]}` (JSON schema enforced) | schema valid; every `quote` is a substring of the draft |
| AGT-6 | Science Auditor | 2 | LLM (mock: rule table by tone) | draft, `world.md` rules, tone | MEM-4 `chNN.science.json` | `{draft, world_rules, tone}` | `{score, issues:[{claim, problem, severity, fix}]}` | schema valid |
| AGT-7 | Length Critic | 2 | **pure code** | draft, `novel` config section | MEM-4 `chNN.length.json` | `{draft, novel_cfg}` | `{score, issues:[{rule, expected, actual, severity, location?, fix}]}` | deterministic; hard violation → score 0 |
| AGT-8 | Summarizer | 2 | pure code (extractive) by default; LLM optional via config | accepted draft, `running.md` | MEM-3 `summaries/chNN.md`, `running.md` | `{draft, running, max_words}` | plain text ≤ cap | ≤ cap words; mentions every entity introduced in the chapter |
| AGT-9 | Style Editor | 3 | LLM (mock: deterministic passes) | all accepted chapters, `characters.md` voice notes, `chars_per_line` | `chapters/chNN.md` (final) | `{chapters[], voice_notes, wrap_width}` | same chapter count; prose wrapped at width | word count changes ≤ ±10 % per chapter; no entity renamed (AGT-5 re-run once as a check) |
| AGT-10 | Publisher | 3 | pure code | final chapters, `synopsis`, config `outputs` | `dist/book.md`, `dist/book.pdf` | `{chapters[], title, synopsis, outputs_cfg}` | valid Markdown; valid PDF (`%PDF-`, resolvable xref) | files exist; nothing else in `dist/` |

**AGT-11 · Uniform interface.** All LLM agents implement `ProducerAgent.run(ctx) -> Markdown` or `CritiqueAgent.run(ctx) -> dict`. Pure-code agents implement the same Protocols so the orchestrator cannot tell them apart. This is what makes AGT-7 and AGT-8 swappable for LLM versions later by config only.

**AGT-12 · Write permissions are typed.** Only AGT-1/2/3 receive a `BibleWriter`. Any other agent attempting a Bible write raises `BibleWriteDenied`. Test TST-6.

