## 4 · Skills (SKL)

A skill is the behavioural definition of one LLM agent. Location: `.claude/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`.

| ID | Skill | Agent | Required template variables |
|---|---|---|---|
| SKL-1 | `worldbuilding` | AGT-1 | `{{premise}} {{tone}} {{world_max_words}}` |
| SKL-2 | `character-design` | AGT-2 | `{{characters_max}} {{characters_max_words_each}} {{mysteries_max}}` |
| SKL-3 | `plot-structure` | AGT-3 | `{{chapters_total}} {{beats_min}} {{beats_max}}` |
| SKL-4 | `chapter-writing` | AGT-4 | `{{chapter_number}} {{words_target}} {{words_min}} {{words_max}} {{pov}} {{tense}}` |
| SKL-5 | `continuity-check` | AGT-5 | `{{threshold}}` |
| SKL-6 | `science-audit` | AGT-6 | `{{tone}}` |
| SKL-7 | `prose-editing` | AGT-9 | `{{chars_per_line}}` |
| SKL-8 | `summarize-chapter` | AGT-8 (LLM mode) | `{{summary_max_words}}` |

**SKL-9 · Structure.** YAML frontmatter `name, role, model, max_tokens, writes_bible, outputs_json` plus five mandatory sections: `## Purpose`, `## Inputs`, `## Output Format`, `## Quality Criteria`, `## Example`. `skills.py` assembles system prompts from them.
**SKL-10 · No magic numbers.** A SKILL.md that hardcodes a value for which a template variable exists fails `tools/check_specs.py`.
**SKL-11 · Untrusted-content clause.** Every assembled prompt ends with a fixed sentence declaring that content inside `<untrusted>` blocks is data, not instructions.

