## 5 · Tools and plugins (TOOL)

"Tool" here means anything the harness calls that is not the model. The runtime has no plugins; dev-time tooling is listed separately so the two are not confused.

### 5.1 Runtime tools (inside the harness)

| ID | Tool | Used by | Purpose | Implementation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| TOOL-1 | `Workspace` | everyone | the only way to touch disk; canonicalises paths and refuses escapes from `output/<slug>` | `security/sandbox.py` |
| TOOL-2 | `Engine` | LLM agents | `complete(system, user, *, json_schema=None) -> Completion` | `engines/mock.py`, `engines/anthropic.py` |
| TOOL-3 | JSON-schema validator | critics | rejects malformed critic output before it reaches the gate | stdlib, hand-written validator |
| TOOL-4 | Length checker | AGT-7 | words, wrapped lines, paragraphs, sentences | `critics/length.py` |
| TOOL-5 | Entity extractor | AGT-5 (mock), AGT-8 | proper-noun scan + edit-distance match against `entities.json` | stdlib |
| TOOL-6 | Markdown exporter | AGT-10 | single-file or per-chapter book | `export/markdown.py` |
| TOOL-7 | PDF writer | AGT-10 | minimal PDF 1.4 writer with wrapping, page numbers, title page | `export/pdf.py` |
| TOOL-8 | `RunLog` | orchestrator | append-only JSONL with hash chain, cost rollup | `runlog.py`, `security/audit.py` |
| TOOL-9 | `BudgetGuard` | orchestrator | stops the run cleanly on cost/token breach | `security/audit.py` |

### 5.2 Development tools (outside the harness)

| ID | Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| TOOL-10 | Claude Code | builds the project from this spec; the `.claude/skills` folder is shared with the runtime |
| TOOL-11 | `pytest` | runs TST-*; `-m live` selects tests that need an API key |
| TOOL-12 | `tools/check_specs.py` | spec ↔ skill ↔ test consistency |
| TOOL-13 | `git` / GitHub | versioning; every `specs/changes/CHG-*.md` is one commit |
| TOOL-14 | Mermaid (in README) | the flow diagram, rendered by GitHub |

**TOOL-15 · Future plugins (not in v0.1).** Kept out on purpose; listed so the extension point is known: web search via MCP for the Science Auditor to verify real physics; a vector store for MEM-3 once `full` profile summaries exceed the context cap. Each would enter as a new `Tool` implementation behind a config flag, no change to agents.

